# Share cards are generated by tools/make_share_cards.py on demand. They are
# large PNGs that change whenever the published figures do, so the generator
# is the thing worth keeping in git, not its output.
product/share/

# Outreach targets and who has already been written to are COMMITTED now, and
# on purpose. These lines used to ignore both, and said this would need
# revisiting once the machine ran on a schedule: "one approach per
# organisation, ever" only holds if the record survives between runs, and a
# scheduled run on a fresh checkout remembers nothing that is not committed.
#
# What made that safe rather than a leak is outreach.team_inbox(). The state
# file used to hold whatever address was found, which could be a named
# employee's own inbox - personal data, in a public repository. Organisations
# are now written to only at a team inbox (employability@, abzworks@,
# contact@) and never at a person, so the file holds public bodies' names,
# the addresses they publish for exactly this, and dates.
